ase in test method 3).\n\nActually, for test method 3's \"CheckEcosystemExtensions() 在某扩展缺失时返回非空切片\", the cleanest Python-verifiable assertion is: the env package's Go tests include a test where a fake pi omits an extension and `CheckEcosystemExtensions()` returns a non-empty slice. I can grep env test files for `CheckEcosystemExtensions`. And run the full env test suite to confirm those tests pass.\n\nLet me settle on this structure. I'll also add structural checks that map directly to the test method and the four responsibilities (since \"四职责 check\" is the name of test 2):\n\nStructural checks (light, mapped to test method):\n1. `internal/env` directory exists with .go files (implied by go test, but explicit is clearer).\n2. env source defines exported: `IsPIReady`, `CheckPIInstalled`, `CheckEcosystemExtensions`, `CheckRickAgents`, `CheckRickHooks`.\n3. env source defines `RuntimeEnv` interface with `Ensure`, `DeployCustomizations`, `CheckReady`, and `piEnv` (from task goal — the \"扩展 seam\"). This is in the goal AND referenced in spec. I'll include it because it's a core deliverable (关键结果 #6) and cheap to check. Actually... hmm. Let me include it but keep it minimal. The test method says \"四职责 check\" and the four responsibilities. The RuntimeEnv interface is the \"扩展 seam\". \n\nActually, let me re-read the Cialdini section: \"每个测试步骤都必须对应明确的验收标准\". And \"测试脚本生成必须覆盖全部验收条件\". The \"验收条件\" (acceptance criteria) in the TDD context = the test method's 预期. I'll map test steps 1:1 to test method's three cases. I'll add structural checks ONLY where they map to explicit test-method assertions (the four check function names, TestIsPIReady, CheckEcosystemExtensions).\n\nI'll include a modest set of structural checks that are DIRECTLY named in the test method (not the whole task goal), to avoid over-coupling:\n\n- `internal/env` exists (package).\n- Env source contains: `IsPIReady`, `CheckPIInstalled`, `CheckEcosystemExtensions`, `CheckRickAgents`, `CheckRickHooks` (test m