{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have everything I need. Let me write the test script.\n\nKey facts confirmed:\n- Module path: `github.com/sunquan/rick`\n- `internal/env` doesn't exist → `go test ./internal/env/...` fails (exit 1)\n- `tools_init_pi.go` doesn't import `internal/env`\n- Current init-pi behavior works (normal path, idempotency, exception all work with fake binaries)\n- Build works\n\nLet me write the Python test script to `/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task3.py`.\n\nThe test will currently produce `pass: false` because:\n1. `go test ./internal/env/... -run TestIsPIReady` fails (package doesn't exist)\n2. `go test ./internal/env/...` full fails\n3. Structural: internal/env dir doesn't exist\n4. Structural: tools_init_pi.go doesn't import internal/env\n5. Structural: tools_theme.go doesn't import internal/env\n\nAnd these are the RED-phase signals (env module not yet implemented).\n\nThe CLI tests (normal path, idempotency, exception) will PASS currently because the current cmd-level init-pi already works. That's expected — those behaviors are being migrated (kept verbatim), not newly implemented.\n\nLet me write the script now."}}
