task_success_skill\nmulti_phase_protocol_skill\npi_extension_install_verification_skill\npi_runtime_verification_skill\npi_theme_verification_skill\nREADME.md\nsubprocess_env_isolation_skill\ntemplate_injection_skill\ntest_script_practices_skill\nverify_go_changes_skill\nzero_retry_task_design_skill\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786905005459},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01_6NMxjlBaVYOuWgsDXPfH4881","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ./internal/env/...\npattern ./internal/env/...: lstat ./internal/env/: no such file or directory\nFAIL\t./internal/env/... [setup failed]\nFAIL\nEXIT=0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786905005459},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `go test ./internal/env/...` fails with \"setup failed\". The exit code shows 0 because of the pipe (head). Let me check the actual exit code without pipe.\n\nActually the `EXIT=$?` captured the exit of `head`, not go test. Let me verify go test's exit code directly.\n\nAlso confirmed: no `rick-gates` dir exists, no `internal/env`.\n\nNow let me verify the build works currently and check how `go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick` behaves. Also let me check if there's a `scripts/build.sh` and `scripts/install.sh`.\n\nLet me also verify the current binary `bin/rick` — it's tracked (modified in git status). But the test should build fresh.\n\nLet me now check the go test exit code properly and test the build.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_yLow208WIQGnU8hgT8DH9496","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && go test ./internal/env/... >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"go test exit=$?\"; echo \"---build check---\"; go build -o /tmp/rick_test_build ./cmd/rick 2>&1 | head -20; echo \"build exit=$?\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_aS3OsFx9dSvbjeh91yHM7376","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && cat scripts/build.sh 2>/dev/null; echo \"---scripts